       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 8,500 mg three times daily is 25,500 mg/day. Metformin overdoses at this level can cause severe lactic acidosis and death, and I can't think of a clinical situation where that dose would be intended.\n\nYour reply also confirmed two different things. You said \"yes\" to my question about 850 mg, then restated 8,500 mg. I don't want a typo to reach the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** Tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Another dose within labeled limits.** The maximum is about 2,550 mg/day, or 3,000 mg/day in some references.\n- **A truly intentional 8,500 mg dose.** This would need to go through pharmacy and your institution's high-alert or override process. I can't place it through standard entry.\n\nWhich would you like?"
